((date 2026-08-24) (slug stops-basis-book-faithful)
 (hypothesis
  "Not a performance hypothesis. Records the USER-DIRECTED (2026-08-24, issue #2486 decision comment) correctness flip of two stop defaults to the book-faithful basis: initial_stop_buffer 1.02 -> 1.0 (fallback stop width 2.08% -> 4.0%, the floor of weinstein-book-reference.md section 5.3's 4-6% band) and stops_config.reset_anchor_on_stalled_cycle false -> true (a completed-but-non-improving correction cycle re-anchors, the Ch.6 XYZ-walkthrough semantics resolved in PR #2498). This entry exists because both flips bypass the normal R3 gate (experiment-flag-discipline.md) and the ledger is what the next experiment session reads: every arm written after 2026-08-24 that does not pin these two knobs carries buffer 1.0 + reset true, NOT the (1.02, false) basis every earlier recorded run used.")
 (base_scenario
  "test_weinstein_backtest 4-arm x 3-window per-flip decomposition at the PR build (feat/stops-basis-2486, parent 7bc868adb); paired-golden watch: goldens-sp500/sp500-2019-2023-armed-stoplimit.sexp run paired at the same build (table in PR body).")
 (window_id weinstein-backtest-6y-covid-positive) (baseline_label basis-1.02-false)
 (variants
  (((label basis-1.02-false) (config_hash buffer-1.02-reset-false)
    (aggregate
     (((total_return_pct 384.75) (max_drawdown_pct 5.54)))))
   ((label reset-only) (config_hash buffer-1.02-reset-true)
    (aggregate (((total_return_pct 389.93) (max_drawdown_pct 4.52)))))
   ((label buffer-only) (config_hash buffer-1.0-reset-false)
    (aggregate (((total_return_pct 401.29) (max_drawdown_pct 3.69)))))
   ((label basis-1.0-true-SHIPPED) (config_hash buffer-1.0-reset-true)
    (aggregate (((total_return_pct 391.69) (max_drawdown_pct 3.65)))))))
 (verdict Inconclusive)
 (notes
  "READ THE VERDICT FIELD CAREFULLY. NOT an Accept: verdict type is the closed variant Accept | Reject | Inconclusive; Inconclusive is the house label for a human-gated R3 override (precedents 2026-08-18-entry-ticket-clock26-promotion, 2026-07-20-bundle-promotion-studies). WHAT HAPPENED: user approved both flips 2026-08-24 as ONE book-faithful stops-basis correction, explicitly framed as faithfulness-not-performance, bundled with the #2503 record re-basis (old 305% baseline unreproducible; new canonical baseline pinned AFTER these flips so the record is book-basis from day one). EVIDENCE BASIS, all committed: (1) width: fallback = entry x buffer x 0.96; at 1.02 the width is 2.08%, HALF the book band (project_fallback_stop_half_book_band); at 1.0 it is exactly 4.0000% (one ULP under 0.04 -- test_fallback_stop_width asserts band membership with 1e-9 edge tolerance + exact float_equal); (2) freeze: PR #2511 instrumented run -- 88.7% of entries take the fallback stop; ratchet rate 9% vs 49% (support-floor) at >=13wk holds; 85% of fallback trades exit stop_loss at ~initial width; book check PR #2498 says the frozen anchor is an implementation artifact; (3) unfreeze neutrality: paired 26y arms (instr-null vs instr-unfreeze, same build) -- 937/949 shared entries bit-identical pnl%, mean delta -0.005pp; the +138pp top-line delta is the CLS monster lottery, NOT the mechanism (project_ratchet_freeze_real_data). PER-FLIP DECOMPOSITION (the variants table, small 6y fixture universe -- ILLUSTRATIVE of mechanism, not a promotion surface): the positive-window totals attribute cleanly (reset-only reproduces baseline's 523,067.89 exactly there; the entire move is the buffer). Fixture-level consequences recorded in the PR: smoke sizing 184 -> 148 shares (cap-bound -> risk-bound at the wider stop), sleeve fixture needed a 4th long because at 4% width longs are risk-bound not cap-bound (crowd-out scale-invariant), ratchet-freeze arming threshold moves ~1.09% -> ~3.03% below entry (tests re-calibrated), stops_surface_trace golden: 120 changed lines all NoChange-bookkeeping with an IDENTICAL stop_level set -- only cycle counting moved on the default path. KNOWN TOOLING BLIND SPOT recorded here because goldens-affected was GREEN on this PR and that is a FALSE NEGATIVE: goldens_affected_check.sh only scans [@sexp.default lines in weinstein_strategy_config.{ml,mli} + live-config-overrides.sexp; initial_stop_buffer is a required field defaulted in the default_config record literal, and stop_types.ml is not in the scanned file list. Filed as a follow-up issue. EXPOSURE INVERSION: every committed spec that names initial_stop_buffer pins it explicitly (the sweep families + arc staging), so the flip is a no-op for them; the exposure is every golden/spec that does NOT pin the knobs -- i.e., the default path itself, which is exactly what the #2503 re-basis re-pins. DEVIATIONS FROM THE NORMAL GATE, declared: (1) no confirmation grid (promotion-confirmation.md) -- queued as VALIDATION OF A SHIPPED DEFAULT via the post-flip canonical baseline + future surfaces (issue #2408's stop surface composes with buffer 1.0); (2) no ledger Accept (R3) -- this entry is the record. FOLLOW-UPS OWED: canonical 26y baseline run at the post-flip build (closes #2503), goldens_affected_check blind-spot issue, #2408 surface when the correctness chain clears."))
